No, you can't. You can only convert from your original alignment, and
only once. (Haven't we done this before? Isn't it in the FAQ or the
beginners' guide?) And the helm of opposite alignment will only make
you chaotic if you're currently lawful; it can't make you neutral.

> The helm fools everyone but your quest leader, I think. 

It does. Even the gods.

> So if you've 
> already done the quest, you should be fine with it if you prefer
> chaotic, but you might as well just stay lawful really. Sacfest for
> Grayswandir!

Seconded. If you haven't done the quest, on the other hand, there's no
way in the world to finish the game because your quest leader won't let
you. You have the choice of quitting, suicide, or trying to get as far
as possible without ascending.

